{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posnbhd","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posnbhd","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":982,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posnbhd","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posnbhd","line":2734,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[a neighborhood of $p$ with strictly positive Hessian]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posnbhd}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity, lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:4.1}\n  There is a neighborhood $V$ of $p$ (inside a normal chart) such that\n  $\\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial t^2}(0,q,v)>0$ for every $q\\in V$ and every unit chart\n  velocity $v$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  $G(q,v)$ is jointly continuous (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity}) and $G(p,v)>0$ for\n  $v\\neq0$ (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter}). Since the unit sphere of chart velocities\n  is compact, the tube lemma produces an open neighborhood $V$ of $p$ on which\n  $G(q,v)>0$ for all $q\\in V$ and all unit $v$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[a neighborhood of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> with strictly positive Hessian] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d312d706f736e626864\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-continuity\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-poscenter\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:4.1</span></span>There is a neighborhood <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V$\">$V$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> (inside a normal chart) such that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\frac{\\partial ^2 F}{\\partial t^2}(0,q,v)&gt;0$\">$\\frac{\\partial ^2 F}{\\partial t^2}(0,q,v)&gt;0$</span> for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q\\in V$\">$q\\in V$</span> and every unit chart velocity <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$G(q,v)$\">$G(q,v)$</span> is jointly continuous (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-continuity\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d312d636f6e74696e75697479\">section 3</a>) and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$G(p,v)&gt;0$\">$G(p,v)&gt;0$</span> for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\neq 0$\">$v\\neq 0$</span> (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-poscenter\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d312d706f7363656e746572\">section 3</a>). Since the unit sphere of chart velocities is compact, the tube lemma produces an open neighborhood <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V$\">$V$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> on which <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$G(q,v)&gt;0$\">$G(q,v)&gt;0$</span> for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q\\in V$\">$q\\in V$</span> and all unit <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-homog","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-homog","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-homog","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-homog"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posnbhd","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posnbhd","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[a neighborhood of $p$ with strictly positive Hessian]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-posnbhd}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity, lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:4.1}\n  There is a neighborhood $V$ of $p$ (inside a normal chart) such that\n  $\\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial t^2}(0,q,v)>0$ for every $q\\in V$ and every unit chart\n  velocity $v$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  $G(q,v)$ is jointly continuous (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity}) and $G(p,v)>0$ for\n  $v\\neq0$ (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter}). Since the unit sphere of chart velocities\n  is compact, the tube lemma produces an open neighborhood $V$ of $p$ on which\n  $G(q,v)>0$ for all $q\\in V$ and all unit $v$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-continuity","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-poscenter","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}